2.
Definitions.
- In these rules unless there is anything repugnant in the subject or context,-
(a)
"the Act" means the Bihar Development of Ayurvedic and Unani System of Medicine Act, 1951;
(b)
"appendix" means an appendix appended to these rules;
(c)
"attesting officer" means a Magistrate or any other Gazetted Officer in the employment of the State Government or in the
Central Government;
(d)
"corrupt practice" means any of the practices specified in Parts I and II of Schedule to these rules;
(e)
"form" means a form appended to these rules;
(f)
"registration officer" or "returning officers, in relation to any matter relating to the preparation of electoral rolls or the
conduct of elections", means the Registrar of the Council;
(g)
"section" means a section of the Act;
(h)
all words and expressions used in these rules and not defined therein and defined in the Act shall have the same
meaning as respectively assigned to them by the Act.
